{
	"description": "Golden vectors for the error window policy of _shared/modules/diagnostics/error_policy.json. signature_vectors: an error's signature is its module, the separator, then the unformatted message template, verbatim. scenarios: each one starts from a fresh session and feeds its events in order; every event is { module, template, at (seconds on the session's clock), enabled (the Debug menu's 'Show a window for every error'), open (the window is open or about to open) } and expects one verdict: disabled (unticked; nothing is recorded), duplicate (this signature already opened or joined a window this session), folded (joins the open window: recorded, spends no budget), rate_limited (max_dialogs windows already opened within the last window_sec seconds; nothing is recorded, so the error may open a window when it recurs later), show (opens the window: recorded and spends the budget). A window opened at time s counts against the budget while now - s < window_sec. The checks run in that order: disabled, duplicate, folded, rate_limited, show. invalid_policies must be refused by validate. Each scenario carries its own policy so the vectors do not move with the production thresholds. Replayed by the macOS and Linux Lua suites (_shared/lua/diagnostics/error_policy.lua) and the AHK suite (windows/infra/error_policy.ahk).",
	"signature_vectors": [
		{
			"id": "module_and_template",
			"separator": "|",
			"module": "keylogger",
			"template": "Flush failed: %s",
			"expected": "keylogger|Flush failed: %s"
		},
		{
			"id": "ahk_placeholders_stay",
			"separator": "|",
			"module": "Menu",
			"template": "Log level {1} was refused",
			"expected": "Menu|Log level {1} was refused"
		},
		{
			"id": "separator_inside_template",
			"separator": "|",
			"module": "a",
			"template": "x|y",
			"expected": "a|x|y"
		},
		{
			"id": "empty_template",
			"separator": "|",
			"module": "mod",
			"template": "",
			"expected": "mod|"
		},
		{
			"id": "non_ascii_template",
			"separator": "|",
			"module": "hotstrings",
			"template": "Échec du fichier « %s » ✗",
			"expected": "hotstrings|Échec du fichier « %s » ✗"
		},
		{
			"id": "other_separator",
			"separator": " :: ",
			"module": "a",
			"template": "b",
			"expected": "a :: b"
		}
	],
